{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-245",
  "title": "Nodebook | Pitch Template",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Nodebook | Pitch Template"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Draft"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> “Hi, I’m [Your Name], and I’m building Nodebook—a programmable productivity platform where your calendar, email, tasks, and notes all live under one roof—and your agents actually understand them."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In Nodebook, everything lives in a unified semantic graph—which we store as a local JSON file that links all your work. The calendar UI is right next to your notes. Your tasks reference emails. Your agents don’t guess—they know."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This week, a tweet with 50,000 views said: *‘I wish I could chat with my calendar.’* That’s exactly the frustration that led me here. Everyone’s bolting agents onto siloed apps—but no one’s rebuilding the application layer itself."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This isn’t just an AI assistant. It’s a new computing environment—where digital context is persistent, programmable, and private by default.”"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Just yesterday, a tweet with 50K views said:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- *‘I wish I could chat with my calendar. Who’s building this?’*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- That’s the problem I’ve been quietly solving for the past year. It started with my own frustration—copying notes between tools, forgetting what I’d said in meetings, juggling tasks my ‘smart’ apps couldn’t connect."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Nodebook is a personal AI workspace where agents operate on your real context—across notes, emails, tasks, and calendar. It doesn’t just assist you—it understands you."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Imagine your calendar could remind you what you promised in your last client call—without you lifting a finger. That’s what Nodebook does."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Nodebook lets an agent read your notes, cross-reference your email, and schedule your calendar—automatically, without prompts."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- I’m building for the 200K+ who already DIY this with hacks. Beta waitlist launches next month to validate conversion."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- I didn’t build Nodebook to chase a market—I built it because I was *suffocating* in the copy-paste grind. Now, the market is starting to catch up. Posts like these go viral every week. The difference? I’m not dreaming about this—I’m already building it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What is Nodebook? (The Elevator Pitch)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Goal:** Investors want a **one-liner** that clearly states what Nodebook is and why it exists."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Pitch:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "*Nodebook is a programmable product ivity platform that lets AI agents operate meaningfully on your personal context—turning scattered tasks, emails, and notes into a unified thinking environment.*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What problem are you solving?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Goal:** Investors want to know if there’s **real pain** in the market."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Pitch:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Right now, knowledge workers waste time manually connecting information across tools—copy-pasting between inboxes, calendars, notes, and AI chats that forget everything. Existing solutions like Notion, ChatGPT, and productivity suites don’t work because they isolate context, forcing users to repeat themselves. Nodebook solves this with a local-first knowledge graph and embedded AI agents that retain memory, automate organization, and surface insights across your digital life."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Why now? (Why is this the right time for Nodebook?)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Goal:** Investors want to know if market conditions **favor your growth**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Pitch:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The shift to AI-native computing is here—but most tools are built for a pre-agent world. As users demand persistent memory, automation, and semantic search, tools like Apple Intelligence tease the future without delivering. Nodebook is positioned to meet this moment with infrastructure that’s agent-first, privacy-respecting, and deeply customizable."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**How big is the market?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Goal:** Investors want to know if the opportunity is **big enough**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Pitch:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The global productivity software market exceeds **$50B**, with prosumers and knowledge workers representing a **$10B+ opportunity**. Even capturing **0.5% of this market** would yield a **$50M+ business**. As the demand for personal AI agents and context-aware automation grows, Nodebook can become the foundational layer of agentic computing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**How does Nodebook make money? (Business Model)**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Goal:** Investors want to see a **scalable, repeatable** revenue model."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Pitch:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Nodebook operates on a **SaaS model**, with pricing tiers from $15–30/month for individual users. Revenue scales through team plans, cloud sync services, and a future agent marketplace. Over time, we’ll expand into enterprise APIs for agent orchestration and cross-context automation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-44",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Why will customers choose Nodebook over competitors?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Goal:** Investors want to know your **unique advantage**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Pitch:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "While tools like Notion focus on content, and ChatGPT focuses on intelligence, neither offers persistent, agent-native context. Nodebook is different: it treats everything as a programmable node, offers full agent access with read/write permissions, and runs on a local-first, privacy-centric sync engine. It’s not just smarter—it knows you."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-49",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What’s your traction so far?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Goal:** Investors want **proof that people care about Nodebook**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Pitch:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-52",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Nodebook was originally built as a personal tool to solve my own frustration with fragmented workflows and context loss across AI tools. While I’m currently the sole user, online communities like r/Notion, r/ObsidianMD, and PKM forums—home to over 200,000 active members—are filled with DIY hacks for AI-powered knowledge synthesis."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-53",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is a massive organic signal: users are trying to bolt intelligence onto tools that weren’t built for it. My go-to-market strategy is to meet them where they are—with a natively agentic alternative that doesn’t require plugins, prompt engineering, or copy-paste workflows. Early traction will come through product demos, community engagement, and GPT-native integrations—focused on creators already pushing the limits of their tools."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-55",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What’s your go-to-market strategy?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Goal:** Investors want to know **how you’ll get customers efficiently**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-57",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Pitch:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-58",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We’re starting with AI-native prosumers—founders, researchers, and operators—via direct outreach, Twitter presence, and thought leadership in agentic computing. We’ll expand via community invites, integrations with popular tools (Notion, Slack, Gmail), and eventually a platform strategy around third-party agents."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-60",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**What’s your long-term vision?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-61",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Goal:** Investors want to see if this can become **a huge company**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-62",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Pitch:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In five years, Nodebook will be the **operating system for personal AI agents**—a programmable layer of memory, reasoning, and automation that sits between humans and their digital world. It won’t just organize your life—it’ll help you understand it."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}